### Dhofar Municipality Portal - example requests
### Works with the VS Code REST Client and JetBrains HTTP Client.
###
### Cookie handling: both clients keep cookies between requests in a file, so the
### session flows below work as written. The CSRF token is readable by design -
### copy it from the dm.csrf cookie into X-CSRF-Token on every mutating call.

@host = http://localhost:4000/api/v1
@csrf = PASTE_THE_dm.csrf_COOKIE_VALUE_HERE
@phone = 91234567
@reference = DHO-2026-A7K2M9

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- health ---

GET {{host}}/health

###

GET {{host}}/ready

### --------------------------------------------------------------- catalog ---

GET {{host}}/departments

### Copy a department id from the response above.
@departmentId = PASTE_DEPARTMENT_ID

GET {{host}}/departments/{{departmentId}}/services

### -------------------------------------------------- public tracking (no auth)

### Returns four fields only: reference, coarse status, submitted, last updated.
### Rate limited to 10 lookups per 5 minutes per IP.
GET {{host}}/public/requests/{{reference}}/status

### ---------------------------------------------------- citizen: sign in ------

### Always answers 202, whether or not the citizen exists.
### With NODE_ENV=development the code is printed to the API console.
POST {{host}}/auth/citizen/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "phoneNumber": "{{phone}}"
}

### Only after the 60-second cooldown.
POST {{host}}/auth/citizen/otp/resend
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "phoneNumber": "{{phone}}"
}

### Sets the dm.cs session cookie. Five attempts, then the challenge is dead.
POST {{host}}/auth/citizen/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "phoneNumber": "{{phone}}",
  "code": "123456"
}

### Remaining idle time comes from the server, not the browser.
GET {{host}}/auth/citizen/me

### -------------------------------------------------- citizen: requests -------

GET {{host}}/citizen/requests?page=1&pageSize=20&status=PENDING

### Idempotency-Key is required. Replaying it returns the ORIGINAL reference
### with 200 instead of creating a second request.
### Note what is absent from the body: departmentId and sectionId. Sending them
### is a 400 - routing comes from the service record.
POST {{host}}/citizen/requests
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Idempotency-Key: submission-2026-09-05-0001
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="serviceId"

PASTE_SERVICE_ID
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Broken street light on Al Nahda street
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

The street light outside building 42 has been out for a week and the road is dark at night.
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="attachments"; filename="photo.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./photo.jpg
------Boundary--

###

GET {{host}}/citizen/requests/{{reference}}

### Only accepted while the status is NEED_INFO.
POST {{host}}/citizen/requests/{{reference}}/replies
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="message"

I have attached the ownership document you asked for.
------Boundary--

###

POST {{host}}/auth/citizen/logout
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### ------------------------------------------------------ staff: sign in ------

### Development password for every seeded account.
POST {{host}}/auth/staff/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "username": "manager.planning",
  "password": "Dhofar#Dev2026"
}

###

GET {{host}}/auth/staff/me

### Rotates the refresh token. Replaying a rotated one revokes the whole family.
POST {{host}}/auth/staff/refresh
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### -------------------------------------------------- staff: operations -------

### Filters are intersected with the caller's scope: they can narrow it, never widen it.
GET {{host}}/staff/requests?page=1&pageSize=20&status=PENDING&sort=-createdAt

###

@requestId = PASTE_REQUEST_ID

GET {{host}}/staff/requests/{{requestId}}

###

GET {{host}}/staff/requests/{{requestId}}/logs?page=1&pageSize=50

### MANAGER and SECTION_HEAD only. The assignee must be active, in the request's
### department, and in its section when it has one.
PATCH {{host}}/staff/requests/{{requestId}}/assignment
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "assignedTo": "PASTE_STAFF_ID"
}

### Pass null to unassign.
PATCH {{host}}/staff/requests/{{requestId}}/assignment
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "assignedTo": null
}

### Moving to NEED_INFO requires a CITIZEN_VISIBLE note.
PATCH {{host}}/staff/requests/{{requestId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "status": "NEED_INFO",
  "note": "Please attach the land ownership document.",
  "noteVisibility": "CITIZEN_VISIBLE"
}

### An INTERNAL note is never returned by any citizen endpoint.
POST {{host}}/staff/requests/{{requestId}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "message": "Applicant has a prior application under review in the archive.",
  "visibility": "INTERNAL"
}

### Scope is derived from the caller's role. There is no scope parameter.
GET {{host}}/staff/analytics/summary

###

POST {{host}}/auth/staff/logout
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{}
